  <div class="method-note-body">CDM dependency and exposure figures: Narrows Chokepoint Dependency Model, HORMUZ chokepoint, commodity codes 2709 (crude petroleum) and 2814, 3102, 3103, 3104 and 3105 (fertiliser: ammonia, nitrogenous, phosphatic, potassic and compound N/P/K respectively), bilateral trade data, 2022&ndash;2024. The fertiliser basket was expanded on 15 October 2026 from nitrogenous fertiliser and ammonia alone to the full basket above. On the nitrogenous-only count, Australia's figures were 38.9% / $789M (Hormuz) and 48.6% / $986M (incl. Oman) on a $2.03B/yr import book; on the full-basket count they are 27.6% / $1.055B and 32.8% / $1.251B on a $3.82B/yr import book.</div>
  <div class="method-note-body">Fertiliser transit shares, Australia's import dependence by nutrient, the Qatar/Gibson Island/Perdaman urea story, and CBA's cost and crop-impact modelling: <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/apr/23/fertiliser-short-supply-australia-farmers-bread-prices-strait-of-hormuz">The Guardian</a>.</div>
  <div class="method-note-body">Japan: first state oil reserve release in four years, <a href="https://english.adnkronos.com/2026/03/26/japan-begins-1st-release-of-state-oil-reserves-in-4-years/">Adnkronos</a>; pump price defended near &yen;170/litre through August, <a href="https://english.adnkronos.com/2026/08/25/japan-to-keep-pump-price-target-at-around-170-yen/">Adnkronos</a>, with a &yen;616bn emergency fund approved in September, <a href="https://www.nst.com.my/amp/business/economy/2026/09/1523364/japan-approves-use-616bil-yen-emergency-funds-gasoline-subsidies">New Straits Times</a>.</div>
  <div class="method-note-body">South Korea: early-March price moves and KEEI's crisis warning, reported via <a href="https://asianews.network/middle-east-tensions-raise-supply-stakes-for-energy-hungry-south-korea/">AsiaNews Network</a> and <a href="https://keia.org/publication/energy-shock-and-economic-resilience-south-korea-and-the-iran-war/">Korea Economic Institute of America</a>; idle tankers, <a href="https://www.koreajoongangdaily.com/business/seven-korean-oil-tankers-stuck-in-strait-of-hormuz-as-government-weighs-options/12518584">Korea JoongAng Daily</a>.</div>
  <div class="method-note-body">New Zealand: Automobile Association's four-dollar-a-litre warning, <a href="https://autotrader.co.nz/news/petrol-in-new-zealand-could-reach-4-per-litre-warns-aa-adviser">Autotrader NZ</a>.</div>
  <div class="method-note-body">Australia: fuel excise relief ending as the conflict pushed petrol prices higher, <a href="https://thenightly.com.au/politics/anthony-albanese-fuel-excise-cut-to-end-as-iran-us-conflict-threatens-petrol-prices-c-22409388">The Nightly</a>; ministerial comment linking the Strait of Hormuz to bowser prices, <a href="https://thenightly.com.au/politics/australian-fuel-prices-strait-of-hormuz-toll-threat-could-impact-amount-paid-at-the-bowser-ted-obrien-says--c-22462297">The Nightly</a>.</div>
  <div class="method-note-body">Thailand: diesel ceiling, export suspension, and the tripled mandatory reserve requirement, <a href="https://www.bangkokpost.com/business/general/3211344/thai-oil-retailers-baulk-at-order-to-triple-reserves">Bangkok Post</a>; Oil Fuel Fund deficit through September, <a href="https://www.nationthailand.com/business/economy/40070569">Nation Thailand</a>.</div>
  <div class="method-note-body">Pump price and policy figures are drawn from national and wire reporting through October 2026 and are each cited to their own reporting date rather than presented as uniformly current.</div>
